Context:

Objective

I work on the Asset-Backed Finance / securitisation desk at a US investment bank in London (Global Markets division).
Our desk:
	•	Provides warehouse financing and securitisation funding to:
	•	mortgage originators
	•	auto captive finance companies
	•	consumer finance lenders
	•	Focus is primarily EMEA ABS / RMBS markets.

Each Monday morning I need to present 3–5 key developments from the previous week at an internal risk-takers meeting attended by trading desks across rates, FX, credit, and equities.

The update should focus on developments and trends relevant to ABS / RMBS / consumer finance collateral, regulatory and general macro news.

⸻

What the weekly report should cover

The assistant should perform a deep search across the previous week using:

Primary sources
	•	Central banks
	•	Bank of England
	•	ECB
	•	Regulators
	•	PRA
	•	FCA
	•	EBA
	•	ESMA
	•	European Commission

Rating agencies
	•	Fitch
	•	S&P
	•	Moody’s
	•	Morningstar DBRS
	•	KBRA
	•	Scope

Financial media
	•	Reuters
	•	Bloomberg
	•	FT
	•	GlobalCapital
	•	Structured Credit Investor

Other industry sources
	•	Law firms (Linklaters, Clifford Chance, etc.)
	•	Trade bodies (AFME, SFIG, etc.)

⸻

Topics that are relevant

1. Regulatory / policy changes

Examples:
	•	securitisation regulation updates
	•	central bank collateral frameworks
	•	capital treatment changes
	•	regulatory consultations

2. Collateral performance

News affecting underlying collateral:

Mortgage / RMBS:
	•	house prices
	•	mortgage rates
	•	arrears / refinancing trends

Auto ABS:
	•	used-car prices
	•	residual values
	•	EV transition
	•	auto loan delinquencies

Consumer ABS:
	•	credit card / unsecured loan performance
	•	consumer spending trends
	•	labour market impacts

⸻

3. Industry developments

Examples:
	•	new ABS / RMBS issuance
	•	warehouse funding trends
	•	ABS conference insights
	•	rating agency research reports
	•	structural innovation (e.g., infrastructure ABS)

⸻

Output format required

The weekly briefing should include:

1. Top 3 developments

For each:
	•	what happened
	•	why it matters for ABS / RMBS
	•	desk implications

2. Collateral performance updates

Short summary of rating-agency research or market data.

3. Primary market / issuance updates

Key ABS deals priced or announced.

4. Short script

A 5–6 line summary I can read in the meeting.

⸻

Scope limitations

Exclude:
	•	CLOs
	•	CMBS

Focus only on:
	•	RMBS
	•	auto ABS
	•	consumer ABS
	•	esoteric ABS where relevant.

⸻

Tone required

The tone should be concise and analytical, similar to a sell-side morning note or internal trading desk briefing.

No fluff — only material developments affecting structured finance markets.